# Project data — sample CSVs, cached API responses, live captures.
# By default nothing under data/ ships with the repo; users bring their own
# input files and any cached responses they want to reuse.
#
# ...with one deliberate exception: the two parcel use-case notebooks ship
# their inputs AND their cached API responses, so they run end-to-end on a
# fresh clone with no API key and no credits spent. A parcel boundary is not
# something a user can invent the way they can invent a point list, and these
# two notebooks are the ones we demo. ~6.9 MB, mostly base64 imagery in the
# satellite / street-view responses.
#
# Note the shape: git will not descend into an excluded *directory*, so each
# level has to be re-excluded with `dir/*` before a file inside it can be
# re-included. `data/` on its own would make every negation below a no-op.
data/*
!data/parcel_diridon_san_jose_sample.geojson
!data/parcel_portfolio_san_jose_sample.geojson

!data/heatmaps/
data/heatmaps/*
!data/heatmaps/heatmap_parcel_*.json

!data/satellite/
data/satellite/*
!data/satellite/satellite_parcel_*.json

!data/street_view/
data/street_view/*
!data/street_view/streetview_parcel_*.json

!data/env_params/
data/env_params/*
!data/env_params/env_params_parcel_*.json
